00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:05.852
In this scene here, we've
got the five senses.

00:11:05.852 --> 00:11:10.080
He brings up smell first,
which is quite common.

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:11.293
When I'm dealing with post-trauma,

00:11:11.293 --> 00:11:14.432
it's normally the smell
that comes out first.

00:11:14.432 --> 00:11:16.016
I'm gonna go for an 8.

00:11:16.016 --> 00:11:19.390
The way that it was drawn
out was quite realistic.

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:21.390
The only thing is, for the viewer,

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:22.945
people who don't know about hypnosis,

00:11:22.945 --> 00:11:24.490
it was quite a quick process.

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:25.380
It's still good.

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:27.670
You have come to the right place.

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:32.290
This is the ideal locale to
lie down and take a rest.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:33.810
Lots of stage hypnotists would do this,

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:36.927
but it's not something
that I would recommend,

00:11:36.927 --> 00:11:37.797
for safety reasons.

00:11:37.797 --> 00:11:39.380
Because if you're gonna make people

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.188
go into hypnosis while stood up,

00:11:41.188 --> 00:11:42.813
the variables are out the window.

00:11:42.813 --> 00:11:44.310
You just can't control it.

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:46.190
You could have people
falling over left and right.

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:48.009
You could have people all over.

00:11:48.009 --> 00:11:50.150
So that's just a safety point for me.

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:52.590
It's important that people
realize that safety comes first

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:53.723
when we're doing any of this stuff.

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:56.752
Jeez, he did it.

00:12:02.377 --> 00:12:05.950
It is quite possible to
hypnotize that amount of people

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.400
at one time and do that.

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:10.580
It is, but it has to be controlled.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:13.151
And I would have more than just me there

00:12:13.151 --> 00:12:14.200
just dealing with that.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:15.883
To have 100% like that,

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:19.544
I'd like to know what happened before,

00:12:19.544 --> 00:12:22.420
but I would expect
maybe five or six people

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:23.870
out of that still to be standing,

00:12:23.870 --> 00:12:24.895
to be brutally honest.

00:12:24.895 --> 00:12:27.600
And I'd give it a 9, because
it is quite accurate.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:29.500
What else makes you feel regret?

00:12:32.439 --> 00:12:33.862
That I did it again.

00:12:33.862 --> 00:12:35.442
One of the misconceptions for hypnosis

00:12:35.442 --> 00:12:37.213
is the therapist couch.

00:12:37.213 --> 00:12:40.713
You do not need to lay
on a therapist couch

00:12:40.713 --> 00:12:41.938
to do hypnosis.

00:12:41.938 --> 00:12:45.263
As for outbursts, it is
quite possible for people

00:12:45.263 --> 00:12:49.123
to sit there and say really dark things.

00:12:49.123 --> 00:12:50.099
You know, you're looking at the person

00:12:50.099 --> 00:12:51.790
and they're saying really terrible things

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.070
and they're laughing at the same time,

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:56.052
which obviously indicates there
is something far more deeper

00:12:56.052 --> 00:12:57.663
and a need for medical support.

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:02.813
Dr. Thurman: What is going to happen?

00:13:06.451 --> 00:13:08.060
Frank is gonna kill.

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:10.140
Is it possible for a client
to get up during a session

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.880
and walk around and grab something?

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:12.730
Yes.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:15.110
Is it possible for a client to self-harm?

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:17.500
Yes, because I've seen it myself.

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:18.930
That, the only thing you do is just

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:20.063
make sure that you reassure them,

00:13:20.063 --> 00:13:21.450
stop them from doing what they're doing,

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:22.750
and just make sure they're safe.

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:27.410
In this scenario, I would
refer this person straight back

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:29.921
to a GP or a physician
straight away anyway.

00:13:29.921 --> 00:13:32.208
Dr. Thurman: If this world were to end,

00:13:32.208 --> 00:13:35.530
there would only be you and him.

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:36.940
I don't touch people in sessions.

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:39.561
There are certain scenarios
when you can use touch

00:13:39.561 --> 00:13:40.873
for making somebody feel like

00:13:40.873 --> 00:13:42.765
they're going deeper into hypnosis.

00:13:42.765 --> 00:13:45.755
I've had people where they've
started grinding their hands

00:13:45.755 --> 00:13:48.083
and started attacking their hands

00:13:48.083 --> 00:13:49.590
and scratching their face as well.

00:13:49.590 --> 00:13:51.360
That's happened in hypnosis sessions.

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:54.107
That's the only time that
I would intervene or touch.

00:13:54.107 --> 00:13:55.500
I'm going to give it a 7.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.850
I mean, bad acting and
a bad therapist, the 7.

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:01.610
The way that the scene
was constructed is right.

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:04.809
It's more theatrics for the
movie rather than realism.

00:14:04.809 --> 00:14:06.701
Elizabeth: I want you to close your eyes.

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:09.495
Simon: We're starting, right?

00:14:09.495 --> 00:14:12.770
Elizabeth: And now your
mind is starting to think.

00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:15.745
I can get hypnosis in under 60 seconds.

00:14:15.745 --> 00:14:19.560
So, I could start hypnosis
with somebody in a room

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:21.687
that's come to see me
who knows I'm a hypnotist

00:14:21.687 --> 00:14:24.280
and have hypnosis in roughly 60 seconds.

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:26.703
60 seconds to three minutes
is what I'm looking at.

00:14:26.703 --> 00:14:28.392
However, it's not just about me

00:14:28.392 --> 00:14:30.350
just getting somebody
who doesn't know who I am

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:31.800
and sitting them down and
saying we're gonna do it,

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.357
because I need time to
educate them and show them

00:14:34.357 --> 00:14:36.686
and get the belief system fired up

00:14:36.686 --> 00:14:38.676
rather than just pouncing
straight into it.

00:14:38.676 --> 00:14:41.484
[cellphone ringing]

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:46.203
It's more of an irritant or embarrassment

00:14:46.203 --> 00:14:48.230
than have any effect on the hypnosis.

00:14:48.230 --> 00:14:50.810
A lot of people think it needs
to be a nice and quiet room.

00:14:50.810 --> 00:14:52.990
That's professionally, we'd like that,

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:53.857
but you don't need it.

00:14:53.857 --> 00:14:54.893
Was I hypnotized?

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:58.139
That's quite an interesting
statement, "Was I hypnotized?"

00:14:58.139 --> 00:15:01.524
That is a very, very
common statement of people

00:15:01.524 --> 00:15:05.660
that have been into
hypnosis and lose time.

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:07.938
They lose time. It's very common for

00:15:07.938 --> 00:15:10.121
if I'm working with people
for around 45 minutes

00:15:10.121 --> 00:15:12.462
to go, "Oh, we've been
doing work for 45 minutes,"

00:15:12.462 --> 00:15:16.880
and they'll say, "45? I thought
I was only in for five."

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:17.800
But, yeah, it's quite common.

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:19.690
That is quite peaceful, as well, to do it.

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:22.197
If I was to give this
movie a rating out of 10,

00:15:22.197 --> 00:15:24.790
because of the theatrics
in it, I'll give it a 6.

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:26.290
There's some realism in it,

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:28.090
but obviously compressed for movies.

